  "verbalization": "Lefamulin is associated with Streptococcal Pneumonia through a chain of indications that link it to Mycoplasma Pneumoniae Pneumonia, which in turn is indicated for Alatrofloxacin and Azithromycin, both of which are also linked to Streptococcal Pneumonia. This suggests a potential pathway where Lefamulin may be repurposed for treating Streptococcal Pneumonia via its effect on Mycoplasma Pneumoniae Pneumonia. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Mycoplasma Pneumoniae Pneumonia across multiple pathways, indicating a possible overlap in therapeutic targets or mechanisms. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications for different pathogens may imply a broader role for Lefamulin in treating bacterial pneumonia, though further validation is needed to confirm its direct mechanism of action in this context.",
